@verbs read reading
@tier player
@title reading what is written

  read <object>

A sign, a plaque, a book, a letter: anything with writing on it is
read by naming it.

Every text is written in some language. If you do not know it, you
see the letters jumbled, and at least learn which language it is
in. Use 'speak' for the ones you know.

Reading is not looking: 'look <object>' tells you what the thing is
like, 'read <object>' gives you what it says.
